# Normalise line endings across the project.
#
# This repo is worked on from both WSL (git with core.autocrlf unset) and
# Windows (git installs default to core.autocrlf=true). Without this file,
# Windows git reports every LF-terminated file as modified because it intends
# to rewrite it as CRLF — phantom diffs with zero line changes.
#
# Worse, a commit made through Windows git would store CRLF endings, and shell
# scripts with CRLF fail inside Linux containers with:
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# eol=lf forces LF in the working tree on every platform, so the shell scripts
# in Fineract/Scripts, Anomaly Detection/Scripts and Fineract/Seeding stay
# executable wherever they are checked out.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the executable content, so intent is obvious on review.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.gradle text eol=lf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.pcap binary
*.rdb  binary
*.tar  binary
*.gz   binary
*.zip  binary
